x86_64-linux  the C1 forms, and nothing about the wrapping this case is for. cxx1 emits C1 and C2 of every constructor and D1 and D2 of every destructor where clang emits only the variants a use asks for - the difference implicit-move.nonames records, unavoidable here because these are the members the *compiler* writes and an implicit constructor is inline by nature with no out-of-line form to switch to. Read the names rather than the count and the point of the case is met on both sides: cxx1 writes _ZZL3onevEN1LC1Ev and _ZZL3twovEN1LC1Ev, two symbols for two types, where before this fix it wrote _ZN1LC1Ev for both and the assembler refused the second definition.
x86_64-windows  the same extra variants, plus the closure type's name: cxx1 spells it $_0 where clang-msvc spells it <lambda_0>, which [expr.prim.lambda] leaves to the implementation and CLAUDE.md already records. The wrapping that this case exists for agrees: ??1$_0@?1??first@@YAHXZ@QEAA@XZ and ??1$_0@?1??second@@YAHXZ@QEAA@XZ carry their own enclosing function exactly as clang's do, where before this fix both were ??0L@@QEAA@XZ.
arm64-darwin  the same as x86_64-linux, the two Itanium targets emitting and naming these the same way as each other.
